  "editorial": {
    "status": "working-edition",
    "notes": "An extended devotional form: the antiphon through Virgo gloriosa et benedicta, followed by Domina nostra and the petitions to her Son. The continuation is attested in Latin prayer books beyond Poland and is not presented as part of the ancient antiphon.",
    "source": {
      "method": "The antiphon was transcribed from the Latin appendix to the Compendium of the Catechism and collated against the Enchiridion Indulgentiarum. The devotional continuation was collated against independent Latin witnesses. The familiar Polish recension was separately checked in historical prayer books from 1883, 1895, 1902 and 1907; the English antiphon was checked in prayer books from 1839 and 1901, while the English continuation is translated directly from the selected Latin.",
      "witnesses": "witnesses/orationes.sub-tuum-praesidium/",
      "apparatus": "witnesses/orationes.sub-tuum-praesidium/apparatus.json"
    },
